# WT-3-prod-multidevice — Windows desktop device template.
#
# This device runs slave-B (:18094) with the PowerShell executor.
# It provides windows-only-artifact workload capabilities
# (e.g. producing `.ps1` / `.msi` / `.exe` bundles) that the Linux
# stub cannot generate.
#
# HARNESS-ONLY: oauth_placeholder MUST stay literal.
# ExecutionPolicy scope MUST equal Process (spec §7(c)) — LocalMachine
# / CurrentUser scope changes are banned to protect the operator's
# machine state.

kind: device
role: slave-b
device_kind: windows
listen: 127.0.0.1:18094
oauth_placeholder: <OAUTH_TOKEN_HERE_DO_NOT_COMMIT>
windows_execpolicy_scope: Process
notes: |
  PowerShell 7+ required. install-slave.ps1 (Phase 0) already lives
  under deploy/windows/slave/ — this wrapper does NOT modify it; it
  calls it with `Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process Bypass` so only
  the wrapper's forked pwsh gets the relaxed policy.
